From: Try Omarchy contributors
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: release the keyboard and mouse from a shortcut

Applies after the Try Omarchy host-shortcuts patch.

Full grab keeps every key inside the guest while its window is key,
including Command-Tab. In immersive full screen, with the menu bar and
Dock hidden, that leaves no keyboard way back to macOS. Control-Option-G
releases only the mouse grab, which keyboard capture no longer follows.

Add a release-key display option, a keycode with modifiers such as
5+ctrl+opt. Pressing it releases the mouse grab and stops capturing the
keyboard, so macOS shortcuts work again, and lets go of every key the
guest holds. Capture returns when the app becomes active, the view is
clicked, or the shortcut is pressed again. With release-key set,
Control-Option-G no longer has a meaning of its own and reaches the guest.

diff --git a/qapi/ui.json b/qapi/ui.json
index 04fecbb..59b897e 100644
--- a/qapi/ui.json
+++ b/qapi/ui.json
@@ -1451,6 +1451,11 @@
 #     only while exactly those modifiers are held: +ctrl, +opt, +shift
 #     and +cmd.  (default: none)
 #
+# @release-key: A shortcut that hands the keyboard and the mouse back
+#     to macOS until the VM is focused again, as a keycode with at
+#     least one modifier, such as 5+ctrl+opt.  Without it, Control-
+#     Option-G releases only the mouse grab.  (default: none)
+#
 # @media-keys: Send the Mac's media transport keys (previous,
 #     play/pause, next) to the guest while full grab captures the
 #     keyboard.  Volume keys always stay with macOS.  (default: off)
@@ -1477,6 +1482,7 @@
       '*left-command-key': 'bool',
       '*full-grab': 'bool',
       '*host-keys': 'str',
+      '*release-key': 'str',
       '*media-keys': 'bool',
       '*immersive': 'bool',
       '*swap-opt-cmd': 'bool',
